$body='<p><strong>Version 2026-09-v1.</strong></p><h2>1. Controller</h2><p>The CampusFR entity responsible for your relationship, as identified at checkout, in your order or invoice, processes the personal data needed for that relationship. General contact: admin@campusfr.fr.</p><h2>2. Data</h2><p>We may process account and identity data, contact details, language, country or market, purchases and access, payment and refund history, support communications, technical and security data, and contractual consent evidence.</p><h2>3. Purposes and legal bases</h2><p>Data is used to operate accounts, deliver content, perform orders, invoice, process payments and refunds, provide support, secure the platform, prevent fraud, comply with legal obligations and manage optional communications where consent is required.</p><h2>4. Payments</h2><p>Payment providers receive the data needed to process payment. CampusFR does not store full card details. Stripe, PayPal, Alfa-Bank or another available provider may be involved.</p><h2>5. Recipients</h2><p>Data may be accessed by service providers strictly needed for hosting, Moodle infrastructure, email, support, security, payments and enabled technical tools.</p><h2>6. International transfers</h2><p>Some providers may process data in several countries. Where required, transfers are protected by appropriate legal safeguards.</p><h2>7. Retention</h2><p>Data is retained for as long as necessary for the relevant purposes and for applicable contractual, security, accounting, legal and evidentiary obligations.</p><h2>8. Rights</h2><p>Depending on applicable law, you may have rights of access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection and portability, and may withdraw consent where consent is the legal basis. Contact: admin@campusfr.fr.</p><h2>9. Cookies</h2><p>CampusFR uses technical cookies and storage needed for sessions, authentication, security and service operation. Optional tools requiring consent are handled under applicable rules.</p><h2>10. Security</h2><p>Reasonable technical and organisational safeguards are used to protect personal data.</p><h2>11. Updates</h2><p>This policy may change. A stable version is associated with the legal documents shown at checkout for traceability.</p>';
